    intro:"The Grade 10 hyperbola is y = a/x + q. It has two separate curves. It never touches its <strong>asymptotes</strong>: the y-axis (x = 0) and the horizontal line y = q. If a > 0 the curves are in quadrants 1 and 3 (relative to the asymptotes); if a < 0, quadrants 2 and 4.",
